Game of Life on sparse tiles (benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m), its process
spawned at the host, on small worlds: tiles start where life reaches them
and end where it dies out, and the population and checksum are those of
the dense programs, life.m and life.c, for the same world and soup
(life.test), as Life is exact. The worlds cover tiles of 4 to 64 cells,
soups from none to the whole world, a side that is not a power of two,
gliders that reach the world's edge, and the pool running out.

Sequential, at -O0 and -O2, and with the loops on the host's threads at -O2.
The -O0 build has no --offload-arch: AMDGPU's code generation at -O0 stops
on its musttail calls in divergent control flow (design document, "LLVM
bugs to report").
REQUIRES: amdgpu-registered-target, libomp
RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m -o %t0
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx1030 %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m -o %t2
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx1030 %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m -o %t.omp

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
A: Game of Life, Mercury, GPU process, sparse tiles
A-NEXT: World: 256 x 256 cells, tiles of 16 x 16, 256 in the pool
A-NEXT: Soup: 64 x 64 cells at the centre
A-NEXT: Steps: 50
A-NEXT: Population: 562
A-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EDGE
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_WORLD=128 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=2000 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EDGE
EDGE: Population: 747
EDGE-NEXT: Checksum: 7031763

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 %t0 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
ODD: Population: 157
ODD-NEXT: Checksum: 2963654

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=100 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE
WHOLE: Population: 4947
WHOLE-NEXT: Checksum: 158368224
WHOLE-NEXT: Active tiles: 1024 at most, 856 at the end

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=64 LIFE_TILE=4 LIFE_SOUP=30 LIFE_STEPS=1000 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
SMALL: Population: 34
SMALL-NEXT: Checksum: 82077

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=512 LIFE_TILE=64 LIFE_SOUP=128 LIFE_STEPS=400 %t.omp host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WIDE
WIDE: Population: 1899
WIDE-NEXT: Checksum: 265191136

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=0 LIFE_STEPS=10 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EMPTY
EMPTY: Population: 0
EMPTY-NEXT: Checksum: 0
EMPTY-NEXT: Active tiles: 0 at most, 0 at the end

Each step's line, for a chart.
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_TRACE=1 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TRACE
TRACE: Steps: 50
TRACE-NEXT: step 0: {{[0-9]+}} tiles, {{[0-9.]+}} s, bookkeeping {{[0-9.]+}} s
TRACE: step 49: 32 tiles,
TRACE-NEXT: Population: 562

RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=10 LIFE_CAPACITY=100 not %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
FULL: The pool ran out of tiles: raise LIFE_CAPACITY.
RUN: %libomp-env LIFE_TILE=6 not %t2 host | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USAGE
USAGE: LIFE_TILE must be a power of two of at least 4 that divides LIFE_WORLD, LIFE_SOUP from 0 to LIFE_WORLD, LIFE_STEPS at least 2, and LIFE_CAPACITY at least 2.
